/-!
# Dickson's conjecture and consecutive primes: consequences

* `Consecutive`: every admissible pattern occurs infinitely often as a run of consecutive primes;
  in particular runs of `k` consecutive primes in arithmetic progression with difference `k!`.
* `Erdos141`: Erdős 141 (`erdos_141`, `variants.eleven`, `variants.infinite_three`,
  `variants.infinite_general_case`).
* `Erdos218`: Erdős 218, `variants.infinite_equal_prime_gap`.
* `BalancedPrimes`: `balanced_primes` and `balanced_primes_order`.
-/
